10:21.010 --> 10:24.010
<b>Starting Life
 in Another 
World With 
My Big Sister</b>

10:28.490 --> 10:31.160
Thanks to Escape and an all-out sprint,

10:30.920 --> 10:33.570
<b>50m Dash: 7.5 seconds</b>

10:31.160 --> 10:33.570
I managed to lose them.

10:34.160 --> 10:36.710
Excuse me. You over there.

10:37.040 --> 10:38.780
Huh? You mean me?

10:38.780 --> 10:40.930
Yes, I mean you.

10:45.330 --> 10:47.680
I was hoping I could ask you for directions.

10:47.680 --> 10:49.870
Oh, of course. Go ahead.

10:53.880 --> 10:57.550
And if you wouldn't mind, 
I'd like you to accompany me.

10:58.250 --> 10:59.170
Escape!

10:59.970 --> 11:02.410
Oh my. Is something wrong?

11:03.220 --> 11:05.450
Wh-Who are you?

11:05.950 --> 11:07.970
You aren't a simple villager, are you?

11:10.650 --> 11:12.810
Are you planning to fight me?

11:13.180 --> 11:14.860
Fight you?

11:16.600 --> 11:18.220
<i>Maya-nee isn't here.</i>

11:18.220 --> 11:21.910
<i>And I don't have enough MP 
to use Escape again right now.</i>

11:23.860 --> 11:27.780
<i>This time, for sure, 
I'll get through this on my own.</i>

11:32.250 --> 11:34.540
Asahi, you're better than I expected.

11:34.920 --> 11:36.040
Huh?

11:36.730 --> 11:39.400
So your experience led you 
to sense my true identity?

11:39.400 --> 11:41.800
That voice... That manner of speaking...

11:41.800 --> 11:43.300
Is that you, Kilmaria?

11:44.210 --> 11:45.800
Correct!

11:45.800 --> 11:48.460
Why are you dressed like that?
 Where are your horns?

11:48.460 --> 11:51.060
It's something called 
perception-blocking magic.

11:55.330 --> 11:59.390
I can control the way others see me and
 make them think I'm a regular village girl.

11:59.390 --> 12:00.690
That's amazing.

12:00.920 --> 12:02.330
I'm just your type, right?

12:03.440 --> 12:05.100
I'm cute, aren't I?

12:06.450 --> 12:10.010
So like creating a character on a sub-account.
 A secondary character, I guess?

12:10.010 --> 12:11.460
What language are you speaking?

12:11.460 --> 12:15.360
What could be so important in this town 
to make you to disguise yourself like that?

12:15.360 --> 12:19.170
I wanted to see humans going about 
their business with my own eyes.

12:19.380 --> 12:20.480
Right...

12:20.480 --> 12:22.670
Show me around town, Asahi.

12:24.180 --> 12:27.850
"Showing a top-ranking officer in the 
Demon King's army around the capital

12:27.850 --> 12:31.180
could be classed as treason."
 Is that what you're thinking?

12:31.180 --> 12:32.890
Don't read my mind!

12:33.110 --> 12:35.700
I told you, I don't have the power to read minds.

12:36.240 --> 12:40.900
After meeting you two siblings, I've developed
 an interest in seeing how humans live.

12:42.190 --> 12:43.530
Is that wrong?

12:44.910 --> 12:49.030
I guess it's fine. I think I can trust you, Kilmaria.

12:50.800 --> 12:52.540
Then, if you would.

12:55.130 --> 12:59.090
You asked me to show you around, 
but I don't know anywhere impressive.

13:00.210 --> 13:01.720
Asahi! Asahi!

13:01.720 --> 13:04.910
There are lots of weak-looking 
humans walking around here!

13:06.290 --> 13:08.680
And some unexpectedly 
large buildings, too.

13:09.110 --> 13:11.940
Makes me want to destroy 
them and clear the land.

13:11.940 --> 13:13.180
Don't do that!

13:14.810 --> 13:17.100
Miss, do you like horses?

13:17.100 --> 13:20.340
I do! And there are magical beasts 
that look a lot like them, too.

13:20.340 --> 13:21.350
Magical beasts?

13:22.810 --> 13:25.040
So this is called a bridge?

13:25.040 --> 13:26.590
You've never seen one?

13:26.590 --> 13:28.490
This is my first time crossing one.

13:31.170 --> 13:33.850
And to think, without this, 
you can't even cross a river.

13:33.850 --> 13:35.500
Being human is so inconvenient.

13:36.160 --> 13:39.580
So inconvenient! So inconvenient!

13:39.900 --> 13:41.650
So inconvenient!

13:47.220 --> 13:49.790
What an impressive view!

13:51.620 --> 13:53.580
Are you thinking about Maya?

13:53.580 --> 13:55.480
You're reading my mind again.

13:55.480 --> 13:57.030
Did you two fight?

13:57.030 --> 13:59.060
It wasn't big enough to call it a fight.

13:59.450 --> 14:03.600
I guess even when you're as close as you two, 
you're bound to annoy each other sometimes.

14:03.600 --> 14:06.990
Well, yeah. I mean, we're human, after all.

14:06.990 --> 14:08.400
Say, Asahi.

14:08.400 --> 14:09.770
Wh-What?

14:10.490 --> 14:11.980
Want to become a demon?

14:13.040 --> 14:14.040
What?

14:15.810 --> 14:17.340
Being a demon is nice.

14:17.340 --> 14:22.540
You're strong and you have useful powers. 
Leave Maya to her own devices and come with me.

14:22.540 --> 14:23.460
What do you say?

14:25.800 --> 14:27.910
I can't leave Maya-nee.

14:27.910 --> 14:28.960
Why not?

14:28.960 --> 14:32.010
Because Maya-nee...

14:32.280 --> 14:33.620
She's not perfect...

14:34.740 --> 14:36.020
but she's family.

14:38.070 --> 14:40.650
Being human is so much work.

14:40.650 --> 14:42.510
They're weak and face inconveniences.

14:43.150 --> 14:44.860
It's just too much work.

14:50.890 --> 14:52.620
Which is why...

14:52.870 --> 14:56.200
I think it'd be better not to open up
 that dungeon to everyone.

14:56.200 --> 14:58.370
Oh, is that so?

14:58.370 --> 15:01.770
It seems like it could easily collapse, 
and if anyone got buried alive...

15:02.630 --> 15:04.340
That would certainly be a calamity.

15:04.910 --> 15:06.580
Are you angry with me?

15:06.580 --> 15:08.090
H-Hey!

15:09.060 --> 15:10.100
Not particularly.

15:10.100 --> 15:12.090
U-Um, this is...

15:13.490 --> 15:16.560
This is your reward for completing the task.

15:16.560 --> 15:18.720
Right. Thank you.

15:22.170 --> 15:24.180
Thank you for your work on this quest!

15:27.920 --> 15:32.360
What'll you do if people get the wrong idea? 
I'd managed to get on good terms with Tanya!

15:32.360 --> 15:34.640
It might not be the wrong idea, you know.

15:35.370 --> 15:38.140
Honestly. You really are 
adorable, aren't you?

15:38.140 --> 15:39.860
Being angry will make you hungry.

15:39.860 --> 15:42.090
Wanna go somewhere 
and get something to eat?

15:43.520 --> 15:46.540
Now that you mention it, 
I haven't eaten in a while.

15:46.540 --> 15:48.030
Here! Thanks for waiting!

15:49.490 --> 15:51.640
All right, let's dig in already!

15:51.640 --> 15:52.720
Wait!

15:52.720 --> 15:56.160
Let's toast. Mine's just juice, though.

15:56.160 --> 15:58.870
Oh, right. What a good idea.

15:58.870 --> 16:03.350
To you, for keeping me 
entertained, and to your sister.

16:03.350 --> 16:05.260
Cheers!

16:11.560 --> 16:12.730
So good!

16:12.730 --> 16:14.950
This is really good, too!

16:14.950 --> 16:18.330
<i>If people found out a top officer 
of the Demon King's army was here,</i>

16:18.330 --> 16:21.630
<i>all of the Guild's adventurers
would probably come to take her down.</i>

16:22.000 --> 16:27.520
<i>If that </i>did<i> happen, whose side 
would Maya-nee and I be on?</i>

16:22.470 --> 16:24.300
Oh, could I get another?

16:24.300 --> 16:27.520
Sure thing! I admire the way you drink, miss!

16:27.520 --> 16:28.500
You do?

16:33.580 --> 16:35.420
Splendid!

16:36.060 --> 16:37.350
I'm completely satisfied.

16:37.350 --> 16:39.190
Okay, let's go, Asahi.

16:39.190 --> 16:40.640
Huh? Oh, sure.

16:42.640 --> 16:46.100
<i>It took a lot to earn this, but...
I guess it's all right.</i>

16:46.100 --> 16:48.190
H-Hey, wait! What about the bill?

16:48.190 --> 16:51.430
Money. You have to pay me.

16:52.440 --> 16:54.330
What's "money"?

16:55.520 --> 16:59.370
<i>Kilmaria-san is the type of person 
who has zero common sense, after all!</i>

16:59.370 --> 17:02.550
Don't mess me around.
Did you plan on eating without paying?

17:02.550 --> 17:05.750
What's this? You want to fight?

17:05.750 --> 17:07.330
Wait!

17:07.330 --> 17:10.220
I'll pay! I'm paying, all right?

17:10.220 --> 17:11.930
O-Oh, are you?

17:17.600 --> 17:20.450
That owner was rather disrespectful.

17:20.450 --> 17:23.180
Imagine demanding 
compensation from <i>me</i>!

17:23.400 --> 17:25.940
Listen up. When in Rome,
you do as the Romans do.

17:25.940 --> 17:29.330
And when you're in this town,
 you must follow human rules!

17:29.330 --> 17:30.050
But...

17:30.050 --> 17:31.870
Do you hear me? You hear me, right?

17:31.870 --> 17:34.040
Yes, fine. I understand.

17:34.040 --> 17:38.660
Why are all the older sister 
characters around me so wild?

17:39.520 --> 17:42.290
Being human really is inconvenient 
and too much work.

17:42.290 --> 17:43.820
You got a problem with that?

17:48.010 --> 17:49.280
What?

17:49.280 --> 17:50.720
Asahi-kun?

17:51.210 --> 17:52.620
Sieg-san!

17:52.620 --> 17:54.060
Are you on a date?

17:54.060 --> 17:56.230
I see you aren't to be underestimated.

17:56.570 --> 17:58.510
A date? Gosh, you're making me blush!

17:58.510 --> 17:59.220
Don't.

17:59.450 --> 18:02.900
I'm Siegfried. Pleased to meet you, miss.

18:02.900 --> 18:03.430
Same.

18:08.510 --> 18:10.920
Asahi-kun, who is this person?

18:10.920 --> 18:14.400
Oh, um, well...

18:16.010 --> 18:19.320
A friend. Just a regular friend.

18:21.280 --> 18:22.650
I see.

18:24.570 --> 18:26.940
I suddenly got a chill and feel dizzy.

18:27.770 --> 18:31.030
I guess I'm not feeling well,
 so I'll head home.

18:31.790 --> 18:33.630
T-Take care.

18:33.630 --> 18:35.060
Glomp!

18:35.060 --> 18:37.510
Let's go to your house and drink some more!

18:37.510 --> 18:38.550
What?

18:40.550 --> 18:42.730
It looks a lot nicer now.

18:42.730 --> 18:45.390
We worked hard cleaning 
the place and making repairs.

18:45.390 --> 18:46.820
Asahi. Asahi.

18:47.330 --> 18:50.760
Shall we put how I look to good use
 and play a prank on Maya?

18:50.760 --> 18:52.080
What do you mean?

18:53.730 --> 18:55.730
Sounds fun. I'm in.

18:56.940 --> 18:58.160
I'm back!

18:58.160 --> 19:01.250
Welcome home, Asahi. Dinner is all prepare—

19:02.170 --> 19:03.870
Pleased to meet you, big sister.

19:03.870 --> 19:07.530
Asahi-kun has done me the 
honor of letting me date him.

19:07.530 --> 19:09.190
My name is Maria—

19:10.810 --> 19:12.380
Maya-nee, how could you?

19:12.380 --> 19:14.630
What are you playing at, Kilmaria?

19:14.630 --> 19:16.330
You could tell?

19:16.330 --> 19:19.880
She may change her appearance, 
but she can't hide her suspicious aura.

19:21.180 --> 19:23.760
I-I'd expect nothing less from my rival.

19:23.760 --> 19:26.940
Who knew you'd see through 
my perception-blocking so easily?

19:26.940 --> 19:29.310
But be that as it may...

19:29.310 --> 19:32.520
What kind of person hits a guest 
with a broom out of nowhere?!

19:32.520 --> 19:34.210
Want to go? Bring it on!

19:34.210 --> 19:37.860
You little...

19:35.250 --> 19:38.530
Don't start rampaging! 
You'll destroy our base!

19:38.970 --> 19:42.400
That's enough of that for today! 
Let's just all be friends!

19:42.400 --> 19:45.030
Well, if you're telling me to, Asahi...

19:45.360 --> 19:48.690
Honestly. Where have you
been this whole time?

19:49.070 --> 19:53.210
Your big sister made a meal 
and waited for you, you know.

19:53.210 --> 19:55.040
Well, I... Thank you.

19:55.040 --> 19:55.790
Look!

19:56.080 --> 19:57.990
Wow, it looks good!

19:57.990 --> 20:02.010
It's been a while since I cooked in an 
actual kitchen, so I ended up going all out.

20:02.010 --> 20:06.170
<i>But I just came from a meal with Kilmaria.</i>

20:06.170 --> 20:08.250
What's wrong? No appetite?

20:08.250 --> 20:09.970
Oh, it's not that.

20:11.190 --> 20:13.220
<i>H-Huh? My stomach...</i>

20:13.580 --> 20:14.900
<i>Is this...</i>

20:14.900 --> 20:17.030
<i>Kilmaria's magic?</i>

20:17.030 --> 20:19.460
Honestly. You do take a lot of looking after.

20:19.460 --> 20:20.820
Now, let's eat.

20:21.740 --> 20:24.060
There's no food for you here.

20:24.060 --> 20:25.910
If you have no reason to be here, leave.

20:25.910 --> 20:27.370
Why?!

20:27.370 --> 20:31.620
Looking after a pet is a lot of work, 
so casually offering to feed one is bad.

20:31.620 --> 20:34.220
Don't go talking about me like I'm a stray dog!

20:34.220 --> 20:36.050
You laughed just now, didn't you?

20:36.050 --> 20:37.730
I don't wanna go! I don't wanna!

20:37.730 --> 20:41.450
I wanna enjoy human food some more!

20:40.090 --> 20:41.800
Are you a kid throwing a tantrum?

20:42.050 --> 20:44.590
Maya-nee, I'd like her to stay, too.

20:44.590 --> 20:46.300
Guess I have no choice, then.

20:46.680 --> 20:48.390
Thank you for the meal!

20:49.860 --> 20:54.810
There's no need to wolf it down.
 This meal I cooked isn't going to run away.

20:54.810 --> 20:57.450
Maya-nee, thank you. I mean it!

20:58.070 --> 21:02.480
Maya-nee's really good at cooking, too. 
She's cooked for me since forever ago.

21:04.720 --> 21:06.950
W-Well, theses dishes <i>look</i> rather good,

21:07.270 --> 21:08.910
but how do they all taste?

21:08.910 --> 21:10.900
You can leave without 
trying any, if you want.

21:10.900 --> 21:12.660
I never said I wasn't gonna try them.

21:12.660 --> 21:14.160
Okay, let's see...

21:19.040 --> 21:21.630
Delicious!

21:26.080 --> 21:27.800
You're pretty good at this.

21:29.210 --> 21:30.830
You're very good at this.

21:31.930 --> 21:34.590
You're incredibly good at this.

21:35.300 --> 21:39.520
If you praise me <i>that</i> much, 
I can't say I dislike it.

21:40.280 --> 21:42.730
But if I don't sample more 
from other meal menus,

21:42.730 --> 21:45.490
I still won't understand 
human meals, you know?

21:45.490 --> 21:47.950
Perhaps I'll come here 
and eat again tomorrow.

21:47.950 --> 21:50.650
How can you say something 
so incredibly shameless?

21:50.650 --> 21:55.710
Don't be so stingy. Making enough for three 
isn't so different from cooking for two, right?

21:55.710 --> 21:58.710
That line's reserved for the 
person doing the cooking!

21:58.710 --> 22:00.980
Well, I want to sample other flavors!

21:59.550 --> 22:03.560
<i>Our meals have become 
very merry and animated.</i>

22:00.980 --> 22:03.560
Then, go sample them somewhere else!

23:36.470 --> 23:37.520
<b>Next Time</b>

23:37.010 --> 23:40.020
Next time: "The Hero and the Big Sister."

23:37.560 --> 23:37.730
<b>Episode 6</b>

23:37.850 --> 23:41.890
<b>Episode 6</b>

23:38.180 --> 23:41.890
<b>The Hero and the Big Sister</b>
